Boost quickbook and boostbook are very good to generate html, pdf, man documents. Boost quickbook .qbk file format is good to write.

boost quickbook: Write Simple Docs .

Requires:

* [link build-install-b2-build  Build and Install B2 Build]
* [link build-install-boost-docs-system Build and Install Boost Docs System: boost quickbook]

[h1:first-init-folders [role cyan First: Init project folders]]

Init project folders:

```
> mkdir foo
> cd foo
```

[h1:next-start-qbk [role cyan Next: Write a start .qbk file]]

[*File: main.qbk]

[!teletype]
```
[book c++ Book
	[id cpp-book]
	[quickbook 1.7]
]

Start, c++

[h1:cpp Hello World!]

Hello, c++

Thanks, website [@https://www.cppfx.tiv.cc cppfx]
```

As you see, you will quickly understand .qbk file syntax.

The title is [role red c++ Book], and the html tag [role red <h1>] will use that title too.

The [role red \[h1] will be translated to html [*<h2>]


[*To avoid keyword c++ to be parsed as c, and let it to be parsed as cpp, define id anywhere.]

[*For example, document id:]

```
[book c++ Book
	[id cpp-book]
```

[*For example, anchor id:]

```
[h1:cpp-text c++ text]
```

[*Then c++ will be parsed as cpp]

[h1:next-write-jamfile [role cyan Next: Write Jamfile]]

[*File: jamroot]

```
xml abc : main.qbk ;

boostbook xyz : abc ;
```

The rule xml defines a target abc, so it will generate file [*abc.xml]

The rule boostbook defines a target xyz, and use previous target abc as its source, it will generate files [*abc.docbook], [*index.html]

[role ddblue
A .qbk file refered in the jamfile will generate the html [*index file: index.html] ;[br]
A .qbk file refered in another .qbk file will generate a html [*subpage], not index.[br]
Read below.
]

[h1:next-build-at-first-time [role cyan Next: Build at the first time]]

Just run command b2:

```
> b2
```

You will see the html document is generated.

[h1:next-qbk-as-subpage [role cyan Next: Add another qbk as subpage]]

[*File: cpp-article.qbk]

[!teletype]
```
[article This is c++ subpage title
	[id cpp-subpage]
	[quickbook 1.7]
]

Hello, c++ World!

This is c++ document

[h1:cpp-text c++ Text]

Hi, I am a room.
```

[*Add subpage to the main page]

A subpage is not written to the jamfile, but written to the main .qbk file: main.qbk

The updated [*main.qbk] will be like this:

[!teletype]
```
[book c++ Book
	[id cpp-book]
	[quickbook 1.7]
]

[include cpp-article.qbk]

Start, c++

[h1 Hello World!]

Hello, c++

Thanks, website [@https://www.cppfx.tiv.cc cppfx]
```

[h1:next-build-again [role cyan Next: Build Again]]

```
> b2
```

[h1:next-install-boost-media [role cyan Next: Install boost media]]

[h2:Update-jamroot Update jamroot]

The html generated above is not so nice-looking, thats because boost media is not installed.

Extract boost c++ library release package, then add the following code to [*jamroot] :

(Please [role blue replace] [*my-path/to-extracted/boost-release] with your real boost extracted folder path.)

[role blue [*Update jamroot :]]

[!teletype]
```
boost-path = my-path/to-extracted/boost-release ;
boost-media-path = $(boost-path)/doc/src ;

install
	boost-media
:
	[
		glob
			$(boost-media-path)/*.css
			$(boost-media-path)/images/*.png
	]
:
	<location>./html
	<install-source-root>$(boost-media-path)
;
```

The rule [role blue install] defines a target boost-media, and use the files of searched by [role blue [*\[ glob ... ]] as its sources, copy the files to location [*`./html/`]

[h2:jamfile-install-source-root [role dddcyan <install-source-root>]$(boost-media-path)]

* [*[role ddred <install-source-root>] means preseriving hierarchical directories.]
* [*[role ddred Its value] means remove this path prefix from source path] , and then [*install them to target path] .[br]
(the property [role dred key] is [*<install-source-root>][br]
the property [role dred value] is [*$(boost-media-path)], aka. [*my-path/to-extracted/boost-release/doc/src])

[h3:without-this-property Without this property:]

`my-path/to-extracted/boost-release/doc/src/` will be[br]
created under target loctation `./html`

and then[br]
all the css and png files will be[br]
installed under [*one folder:][br]
`./html/my-path/to-extracted/boost-release/doc/src/`

[h3:with-this-property With this property:]
the *.css files will be installed under `./html/`[br]
and the *.png will be installed under `./html/images/`

[h1:btw-jamfile-property [role cyan BTW.: Jamfile property]]

* [* [role dred Property]]
* [* [role dred Property key]]
* [* [role dred Property value]]

A property of b2 jamfile has a [*key] and a [*value]

[h3 Property Example:]

`<include>/usr/include`

The above line is a [role dred [*property]],[br]
the [role dred property [*key]] is `<include>`[br]
the [role dred property [*value]] is `/usr/include`

[h3 More property Examples:]

`<cxxflags>"-I/usr/include -freflection"`

`<define>__my_debug__`

`<link>shared`

[h1:next-build-again [role cyan Next: Build again]]

```
> b2
```

